      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would be a neat feature, but it could also be taken advantage of by malicious people.\nAn idea I had for this is for there to be a button to get in a call with emergency services depending on which country they're from. (Not to include their private address into their account for privacy reasons).\nWhen they get into the call with emergency services, their mic would go into immediate mute so that they can give information to the emergency services without revealing it to the public.\nOr if emergency services are not what they prefer to call, they could set up the button to call a different number (their parents, roommates or partners); so that they can get a direct assistance.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-12-21T09:55:36.212Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRC extremely needs emergency support that will help person to contact emergency services of his country for help or in extreme situations call 911. Yesterday I was about to lose my friend due to the fact that he almost got overdosed by the pills that doctor gave him against depression and some other serious issues I am not allowed to speak about. No one knew his address and he was weak to move and get the phone. He is fine now, thankfully we sorted things out. If it wasn't for low dose of medicine everything would end not so well. Statistically VRC has a lot of users who are suffering from depression and different types of mental issues and they use VRC to cope with it or feel better. But due to the fact that things may get out of the hand this functionality should be inseparable feature of VRC because no one is insured from this kind of hazards. Hope VRC developers will look to this situation with responsibility and do some progress in that direction.",
